Implemented a singly linked list (LIFO stack) in `simple_linked_list.py`:

- `Node` — stores `_value`/`_next`, exposes `.value()` / `.next()`
- `LinkedList` — `__init__(values)` pushes each value (last becomes head), `__len__`, `__iter__` (head→tail), `head()`, `push()`, `pop()`, and `reversed()` (returns a new list built from the current one)
- `EmptyListException` raised with exact message `"The list is empty."` on `head()`/`pop()` of an empty list

